    <briefdescription>
<para>Ascon-XOF128 extendable-output function. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>An extendable-output function (XOF) generalises a hash function by allowing the caller to request a digest of any desired byte length rather than a fixed-size output. ASCON-XOF128 realises this construction through a sponge operating over a 320-bit permutation state, absorbing the padded message in 64-bit rate blocks and squeezing an arbitrary number of output bytes through repeated applications of the Ascon-p permutation, as standardised in NIST SP 800-232.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ulink url="https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-232">https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-232</ulink></para>
</simplesect>
